  "Solution": "This is the sum of the coefficients of \\((a+b)^4\\), which equals 16.\n\nAlternative method 1: Evaluate the combination numbers\n\nThe five small combination numbers can be evaluated directly. The combination formula gives \\(C(4,0)=1\\), \\(C(4,1)=4\\), \\(C(4,2)=\\frac{4\\cdot3}{2\\cdot1}=6\\), \\(C(4,3)=4\\), and \\(C(4,4)=1\\). Adding these values gives\n\\[\n1+4+6+4+1=16.\n\\]",
